<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Keep committee-keeper.mjs --watch resident.

     WHY THIS EXISTS, measured on 2026-09-04.

     The keeper process died at roughly 23:05 local on 09-03 and was still not running eleven hours
     later. 52 consecutive epochs went unpinned, which fail-closed committee validate() for 53 of them
     (validate() needs BOTH `e` and `e-1`), on the morning of the CC-115 B3 evidence run.

     Nothing was broken except the absence of this file. The alerting worked perfectly: the health
     agent fired every 15 minutes and appended to issue #305 forty-five consecutive times. The host was
     awake. The three DVT node containers were `Up 2 days (healthy)` the entire time. The ONLY thing
     missing was something to start the process again -- the monitoring was complete and the monitored
     process had no supervisor, so the outage was fully observed and fully unattended.

     That is a different failure from the eight before it. Those were host sleep (clamshell on AC,
     maintenance sleep on battery -- `caffeinate` covers neither), each self-healing on wake within
     k<=3 epochs. This one could not self-heal, because a dead process does not wake up with the
     laptop.

     KeepAlive, NOT StartInterval. This supervises a RESIDENT process; the other two agents in this
     directory run a periodic job and exit. That difference changes how you verify it -- see below.

     ThrottleInterval 30: if the keeper is crashing on startup (bad RPC, missing key), relaunching it
     ten times a second turns a configuration error into a spend. 30s still recovers a real crash well
     inside one epoch (64 blocks ~= 12.8 min).

     VERIFY DIFFERENTLY FROM THE OTHER TWO. `launchctl print` will NOT show a `run interval` line here
     -- correctly, there is no interval. Read `state` and `pid` instead:

         launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/io.aastar.dvt-committee-keeper | grep -E "state|pid|last exit"
         #   state = running        <- what matters
         #   pid = NNNNN

     And do not stop at "launchd says running" -- that was never the failing question. Ask the chain:

         node scripts/check-pin-rate.mjs --blocks 600     # recent epochs, misses grouped into runs

     Install: deploy/README-heartbeat.md -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>io.aastar.dvt-committee-keeper</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/jason/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin/node</string>
    <string>/Users/jason/Dev/aastar/YetAnotherAA-Validator/deploy/committee-keeper.mjs</string>
    <string>--watch</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/jason/Dev/aastar/YetAnotherAA-Validator</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/jason/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/jason</string>
    <!-- The ROUTER, not a validator address. Resolving algId 0x01 through the router every run is what
         keeps this agent from becoming the next thing pinned to a retired contract (#283). -->
    <key>COMMITTEE_ROUTER</key>
    <string>0xA97A752779ebfDA58612F6727Ec7C8366c39f897</string>
    <!-- The validator's creation block. Without it the keeper rebuilds the active set by scanning
         `eth_getLogs` FROM BLOCK 0 on every single pin, which took ~5 minutes per epoch on Sepolia and
         is most of the "steady state" unavailability that check-pin-rate reports: pin offsets of 24,
         26 and 40 blocks into a 64-block epoch, during every one of which committee ops fail closed.
         The keeper warns about this on stdout and the warning had been scrolling past unread.

         Verified in BOTH directions rather than taken from the E2E driver's bisection: eth_getCode at
         11599098 returns 0x, at 11599099 returns 46956 hex chars. -->
    <key>DEPLOY_BLOCK</key>
    <string>11599099</string>
  </dict>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jason/Dev/aastar/YetAnotherAA-Validator/deploy/.run/committee-keeper.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jason/Dev/aastar/YetAnotherAA-Validator/deploy/.run/committee-keeper.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
